<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto of Warcq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otto of Warcq is the first known count of Chiny, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardennes">Ardennes</a> of present-day southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, in the later 10th century. He built a castle at Chiny on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semois">Semois</a> river, and his descendants extended the county towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carignan-ardennes">Ivoix</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montmedy">Montmédy</a>. The county stayed in their family until the 13th century, when it passed by marriage to the counts of Looz.</p></div>
